            "review_title": "Review at Lan Rung",
            "review_text": "Darwinflashpacker\n28 contributions\n0\nTasty Vietnamese food\nJan 2025 • Couples\nWe stumbled upon this place by accident. It’s in a large, open courtyard with an extensive menu. Although the staff had limited English, and we have no Vietnamese, and despite some initial confusion, we ended up having a lovely dinner here. I had fried chicken wings in fish sauce and my partner had Schezwan prawns. Both dishes were very good. As with many Vietnamese restaurants, things placed on your table without you asking (wet wipes, peanuts, pickled vegetables) are not free, but you’ll only be charged if you eat them, so if you don’t want to pay for them, just leave them alone. This is a lovely setting to eat Vietnamese food in Vung Tau.\nRead more\nWritten January 26, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
