            "review_title": "Review at Lan Rung",
            "review_text": "Loh K W\nSingapore, Singapore1060 contributions\n0\nGreat atmosphere and good food\nFeb 2018 • Family\nWe had a long table for 20 of us arranged by the beach side. The night was cool with a constant wind blowing. I dare not think what will happen if it rain. We walked around this large restaurant and noticed it was quite full with many happy diners. \n\nThe atmosphere was great for a fun and casual dinner. As with a normal Asian dinner, we shared the many dishes we ordered. As we have a vegan guest, a vegetarian soup was ordered. The soup was delicious and the vegetables were fresh. A fried lemon grass tofu dish was ordered for her. It must be the best fried tofu I have eaten. The slight lemon grass flavour made this dish very special. It was crispy on the outside and soft inside. The tofu flavour was rich and aromatic. Please see the photographs on the other dishes we ordered.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 3, 2018",
