            "review_title": "Review at Lan Rung",
            "review_text": "Courtney I\nWanneroo, Australia74 contributions\n0\nGood and bad\nJan 2018\nWe left this hotel today a day early than paid and booked for, to many stairs, a massive hill to get to reception, the pool/spa/massage/breakfast area is on the other side of the road where there is another part of the hotel with a see view and more rooms, not wheelchair or disabled friendly, no hot water, water cut off, few power cuts, anyone can pay to use the pool from elsewhere, breakfast is definitely not suitable for Europeans as they only serve Vietnamese foods for breakfast, but they had lovely rooms, comfy beds, excellent view from the pool when you’re there but watch as the ocean waves come over the side of the wall near pool soaking around 5/6 of the sun beds, my parents wouldn’t stay here again due to there age and having to walk up a million flight of stairs just to get to there room and I wouldn’t stay here again due to having to cross the road to the pool and breakfast, I prefer walking out of my room just a few steps to the pool and breakfast!!\nRead more\nWritten January 7, 2018",
